# Founders OS MCPB exclusions
#
# mcpb pack already excludes by default: .git, .DS_Store, *.map, *.log,
# node_modules/.cache, node_modules/.bin, package-lock.json, .npmrc, .env.local
#
# Everything below is additional pruning of the production install tree.
#
# PRUNE CAREFULLY. Some packages ship runtime JSON, WASM, or certificate
# bundles under paths that look like documentation or examples. After adding
# any pattern here, re-run the cold-start smoke test (runbook section 8)
# before shipping. A larger bundle beats a broken one.

# Docs and sources that never execute.
#
# NOTE: LICENSE / LICENCE / NOTICE files are deliberately NOT excluded.
# This bundle redistributes its dependencies, and MIT, BSD, and Apache-2.0
# all require the license text to travel with the code. Stripping them to
# save a few hundred kilobytes would put the artifact out of compliance.
**/*.md
**/*.markdown
**/CHANGELOG*
**/*.ts
**/*.tsx
**/*.flow

# Test and CI material from dependencies
**/__tests__/
**/test/
**/tests/
**/*.test.js
**/*.spec.js
**/.github/
**/.circleci/
**/coverage/

# Editor and tooling noise
**/.editorconfig
**/.eslintrc*
**/.prettierrc*
**/tsconfig*.json
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/

# Icon sources and the rasterizer are authoring inputs, not runtime assets.
# The committed PNGs they produce are what the manifest references.
assets/*.svg
assets/generate-icons.mjs
assets/screenshots/
